  "training": {
    "hints": [
      "Translate the lesson into explicit state and permissive logic: The elevator receives one direction command only when the doors are closed and the landing is clear.",
      "Inputs are simulator feedback (call_valid, doors_closed, landing_clear); PLC logic owns lift_up_cmd, lift_down_cmd.",
      "Test the initial state, the valid condition, and at least one missing permissive.",
      "Car displacement follows one PLC direction command while the three manual permissives agree and the modeled doors have finished closing. Floor flags derive from modeled car position. The manual doors_closed fixture selects one-second sliding-door travel; Stop freezes the pose and Reset opens the doors at home. Modeled closure is not hardware protective sensing.",
      "The new drum, car-roof anchors and changing rope length illustrate a connected hoist path. Rear upper stairs and side lower steps connect landings to floor; access gate is fixed open, without fabricated feedback or an engineered personnel-safety claim."
    ],
    "solution": {
      "summary": "This is an original functional reference for the control concept, not a copy of the photographed solution.",
      "steps": [
        "Require the documented inputs: call_valid, doors_closed, landing_clear.",
        "Command the documented outputs: lift_up_cmd, lift_down_cmd.",
        "Remove PLC commands when the permissive is lost."
      ],
      "acceptance": "The elevator receives one direction command only when the doors are closed and the landing is clear."
    },
    "assetRequirements": [
      "elevator car/shaft",
      "floor call station",
      "landing door",
      "floor-position sensor"
    ],
    "machineGuide": {
      "purpose": "A lift travels between two landings only with door, position, and direction interlocks satisfied.",
      "startConditions": [
        "The common PLC/watchdog foundation is healthy.",
        "All required simulator inputs are at their documented initial state."
      ],
      "normalSequence": [
        "Apply the requested input condition.",
        "Verify only the documented PLC outputs respond."
      ],
      "stopBehavior": [
        "Removing the permissive removes PLC-owned commands.",
        "Reset returns the module to its initial state."
      ],
      "faultBehavior": [
        "A missing or stale input must fail safe and remain diagnosable."
      ],
      "expectedObservations": [
        "The elevator receives one direction command only when the doors are closed and the landing is clear."
      ]
    },
